Title: BLUE CRAYON
Credit: Version B — "The Blue Sun"
Draft: Short cut · 13 October 2026
Notes: Running time 0:51 · No dialogue

FADE IN:

INT. LIVING ROOM - DRAWING CORNER - DAY

Grey morning. Dust hangs in the light.

A wall covered in crayon drawings. Below it, a low kid's table and two small chairs. One is empty.

In the other sits THE ROBOT. Sage-mint paint, rust, a dent in its egg-shaped head. A blue crayon is taped to one finger.

Under the table, a red ball. Flat.

!FLASH.

Warm lamplight. A piano plays four notes. THE BOY (5, curly black hair, mustard hoodie) giggles and tapes the crayon to the Robot's finger.

RRRIP.

!PRESENT.

Silence. PAPA (30s, short black beard) walks past in a black suit. He doesn't look at the Robot.

He goes into the Boy's room. The door shuts.

!FLASH.

Papa points at the Robot. The Boy stands in front of it, arms spread wide, chin trembling.

!FLASH.

Dusk. Boy and Robot asleep together on a pile of drawings.

!PRESENT.

On the table, under the tape roll: one last drawing. Unfinished.

Three figures holding hands under a sun, half coloured in yellow. The yellow crayon lies beside it.

The Robot reaches for the yellow crayon. Its stubby fingers can't hold it. It slips. It slips again.

There is no one to tape it on.

The Robot looks at the blue crayon on its finger.

Slowly, carefully, it colours in the rest of the sun. Blue.

INT. HALLWAY - NIGHT

Dark. The Robot's eye-glow is the only light.

It pushes open the Boy's door.

INT. BOY'S BEDROOM - NIGHT

Papa sits on the floor against the small empty bed. His suit jacket lies crumpled beside him.

The Robot holds out the drawing.

Papa doesn't look.

The Robot waits.

The glow of its eyes falls on the paper. He looks.

!INSERT - THE DRAWING

PAPA, the first P backwards. A small boy: ME. A little round robot. Holding hands.

Above them, the sun. Half careful yellow. Half wobbly blue, scribbled past the lines.

!BACK TO SCENE

Papa's jaw clamps. Holds.

It breaks. He pulls the Robot into his chest and sobs.

!OVER PAPA'S SHOULDER

The Robot, chin on his shoulder. Arms at its sides. The drawing hangs from its taped hand.

Its eyes stay wide. Still. Fixed on the empty bed.

MUSIC: the four notes. Only three play.

> CUT TO BLACK.

>BLUE CRAYON<

>THE END<
